    "chunk_text": "of small Industrial Workshops\n\nand Management\n\n20,000,000.00 5,000,000.00 10,00,000.00 6,000,000\n\nA.A.C.J. Rajarathna, Governor, Sabaragamuwa Province. 04th day of April, 2025.\n\nEOG 06 - 0144-1\n\nAUTHORIZATION\n\nI do hereby grant permission to the Chief Secratary and the Accounting Officers of the Sabaragamuwa Provincial Council to spend a sum of Sixty Two Billion Two Hundred Eight Million Fifty Five Thousand Eighty Two and Twelve Cents only (Rs. 62,208,055,082.12) out of the Sabaragamuwa Provincial Council Fund, which is estimated for the expenses of the Sabaragamuwa Provincial Council for the one year period that starts on 01st of January, 2025 and end on 31st of December, 2025.\n\nIV ^w& fldgi \u2013 Y%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h \u2013 2025'06'18Part IV (A) \u2013 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 18.06.2025\n\n9A\n\nThis permission will be valid till 31st of December, 2025 or upto the date that expires three months (03) from the date of summoning the Seventh (07th) Sabaragamuwa Provincial Council or from the date re-start the functions of the Sabaragamuwa Provincial Council which occurs first. A.A.C.J. Rajarathna, Hon. Governor, Sabaragamuwa Province. 04th day of April, 2025.\n\nEOG 06-0144/2\n\nAUTHORIZATION\n\nFor 2024 Advanced Accounts\n\nI do hereby approve to amend the advance account limits for the year 2024 stated in the Sixth Schedule of the First Supplementary Financial Statement for the year 2025, by virtue of powers vested in me under Section 27 (a) of the Provincial Council Act, No. 42 of 1987, as the term of the 06th Sabaragamuwa Provincial Council of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka ended on 26th September, 2017.\n\nAccordingly, I do hereby grant permission to the Chief Secretary and the Accounting Officers of the Sabaragamuwa Provincial Council to bear the expenses subject to those limits.\n\nA.A.C.J. Rajarathna, Governor, Sabaragamuwa Province. 04th day of April, 2025.\n\nEOG 06-0144/3"
