    "chunk_size_bytes": 1575,
    "chunk_text": "GRANTING PERMISSION BY VIRTUE OF POWERS VESTED IN ME UNDER SECTION 27(A) OF PROVINCIAL COUNCIL ACT, NO. 42 OF 1987 AS THE TERM OF THE SIXTH SABARAGAMUWA PROVINCIAL COUNCIL OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA ENDED ON 26TH SEPTEMBER, 2017\n\nBE it enacted by me, the Governor of the Sabaragamuwa Province of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka as follows.\n\n1. I do hereby grant permission unto the Chief Secretary and the Accounting Officers of the Province to spend Rupees Sixty one billion seven hundred thirty eight million one hundred and thirty eight thousand only, (Rs. 61,738,138,000/-) and which estimated for the services of the Sabaragamuwa Provincial Council for the One year duration beginning on 01st January, 2025 and ending on 31st December, 2025, by virtue of powers vested in me under section 27(A) of Provincial Council Act, No. 42 of 1987 as the term of the Sixth Sabaragamuwa Provincial Council ended on 26th September, 2017.\n\n2. (1). Without prejudice to any other law authorizing any expenditure of the Sabaragamuwa Provincial Council which estimate will be Rupees Sixty one billion seven hundred.\n\n5. The debit balance, outstanding at the end of financial year 2025 of any activity specified in column (iv) of the second schedule to this order shall not exceed the maximum limit specified in the corresponding entry in column (vii) of that schedule, and the total liabilities of that activity at the end of that financial year shall not exceed the maximum limit specified in the corresponding entry column (viii) of that schedule."
  },
