    "chunk_text": "5. The debit balance, outstanding at the end of financial year 2025 of any activity specified in column (iv) of the second schedule to this order shall not exceed the maximum limit specified in the corresponding entry in column (vii) of that schedule, and the total liabilities of that activity at the end of that financial year shall not exceed the maximum limit specified in the corresponding entry column (viii) of that schedule.\n\n7. (1). Any money which, by virtue of the provisions of the first schedule to this order, have been allocated to recurrent expenditure under any programme appearing under any head specified in that schedule but have not been expended or may likely to be unexpended, may be transferred to the allocation of recurrent expenditure or capital expenditure under any other programme within that head by order of the Chief Secretary to the Sabaragamuwa Provincial Council or any other officer authorized by him.\n\nGranting Permission.\n\nAppropriation for the year 2025.\n\nAdvance payments out of Provincial Council fund or any other fund for the activities mentioned in the paragraph 3 during the year 2025.\n\nPower to transfer unexpected monies allocated to recurrent expenditure to another allocation within some programme or to another programme under the same head of expenditure\n\nIV ^w& fldgi \u2013 Y%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h \u2013 2025'06'18Part IV (A) \u2013 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 18.06.2025\n\n3A\n\n(2). Any money allocated to capital expenditure under any programme appearing under any head specified in the first schedule to this order shall be transferred out of that programme or project only by the Chief Secretary of Sabaragamuwa Provincial Council.\n\n8. (1). That the receipts from taxes and other sources will be less than the amount anticipated to finance authorized expenditure. Or;\n\n(2). That amount originally appropriated for a particular purpose or purposes are no longer required;"
