    "chunk_text": "1. CINEC Campus (Private) Limited shall, when admitting students for the degree programme specified in schedule II hereto in respect of the Bachelor of Science Honours in Computer Science in Network Security and Forensics complete with a minimum of 120 Credits (SLQF Level 6), adhere to the minimum entry qualification of;\n\na. At least three (3) simple passes (S) in Physical Science stream or Engineering Technology stream in one and the same sitting at the G. C. E. (Advanced Level) Examination conducted by the Department of Examinations of Sri Lanka or Equivalent Qualification: or\n\nb. At least three (3) simple passes (S) in any stream in one and the same sitting at the G. C. E. (Advanced Level) Examination conducted by the Department of Examinations of Sri Lanka or equivalent qualification and a Credit pass (C) in Mathematics at the G. C. E. (ordinary Level) Examination conducted by the Department of Examinations of Sri Lanka or equivalent qualification and the successful completion with a bridging programme approved by specified Authority : or\n\nc. At least three (3) simple passes (S) in any stream in one and the same sitting with a simple pass (S) for information and Communication Technology, in any attempt at the G. C. E. (Advanced Level) Examination conducted by the Department of Examinations of Sri Lanka or equivalent qualification and a Credit pass (C) in Mathematics at the G. C. E. (Ordinary Level) Examination conducted by the Department of Examinations of Sri Lanka or equivalent qualification.\n\n2. The institute shall be subject to the fulfilment of the required research capacity within two years from the date of granting Degree Awarding Status.\n\n3. CINEC Campus (Private) Limited is recognized to offer the degree specifed in Schedule II hereto subject to the five (5) year review conducted by the specified Authority.\n\nSchedule II"
