    "chunk_text": "(d) by the repeal of sub-subparagraph (g) of subparagraph (1) and the substitution therefor of the following: -\n\n\u201c(g) Two members elected from among the permanent sta\ufb00 of the Institute engaged in teaching other than the members mentioned in paragraph (f); and\n\n(h) The Senior Assistant Librarian or the Head of the Library of the Institute, as the case may be.\u201d;\n\n(e) by the substitution in subparagraph (3) for the word and \ufb01 gure \u201cparagraph 11\u201d of the word and \ufb01 gure \u201cparagraph 10\u201d; and\n\n(8) by the repeal of paragraph 14 thereof and the substitution therefor of the following: -\n\n\u201c14. (1) There shall be Departments of Study in respect of the disciplines of-\n\n(a) Carnatic Music; (b) Dance, Drama and Theatre Arts; (c) Visual and Technological Arts; and (d) Information Technology.\n\n(2) Each Department of Study shall have a Head of Department who shall be a Senior Professor, Professor, Associate Professor or Senior Lecturer and shall be appointed by the Board upon the recommendation of the Director.\n\n(3) The Head of a Department shall hold o\ufb03 ce for a period of three years reckoned from the date of his appointment and shall, unless removed from o\ufb03 ce, be eligible for reappointment.\n\n(4) Where owing to leave of absence, illness, or other cause, the Head of a Department is temporarily unable to perform the duties of his o\ufb03 ce for a period not exceeding three months, the Board shall appoint a Professor, Associate Professor or Senior Lecturer to act in the post of Head of Department for such period. Where however a Head of a Department retires or resigns, or is for other reasons is unable to perform the duties of his o\ufb03 ce for a period exceeding three months, the post of Head of Department shall be deemed to be vacant, and a new Head of Department shall be appointed in accordance with subparagraph (2).\u201d.\n\nEOG 06 - 0125\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA."
