    "chunk_text": "12B. (1) A Board of Study shall consist of the following persons: -\n\n(a) all permanent teachers of the Institute who are teaching in the respective degree, diploma or the certificate programme and who have been confirmed in their appointment; and\n\n(2) The Chairperson and the Secretary of the Board of Study shall be appointed from among the members referred to in sub-subparagraph (a) of subparagraph (1).\n\n(3) The respective Board of Study shall plan, implement and evaluate the taught degree, diploma or certificate course or the taught degree with a research component and shall be accountable to the Academic Committee in its planning, implementation and evaluation.\u201d;\n\n(10) by the repeal of paragraph 20 thereof and the substitution therefor of the following:-\n\n\u201c20. In this Ordinance -\n\n\u201cAct\u201d means the Universities Act, No. 16 of 1978;\n\n\u201cappropriate Instrument\u201d shall have the same meaning as assigned to that term in the Universities Act, No. 16 of 1978;\n\n\u201cby-law\u201d shall have the same meaning as assigned to that term in the Universities Act, No. 16 of 1978;\n\n\u201cHigher Degrees\u201d means MPhil (Master of Philosophy) and PhD Doctor of Philosophy) conducted by the Institute and awarded by the University;\n\n\u201cHigher Educational Institution\u201d shall have the same meaning as assigned to that term in the Universities Act, No. 16 of 1978;\n\n\u201cteacher\u201d shall have the same meaning as assigned to that term in the Universities Act, No. 16 of 1978; and\n\n\u201cUniversity Grants Commission\u201d means the University Grants Commission established under section 2 of the Universities Act, No. 16 of 1978.\u201d EOG 06 - 0124\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA."
