    "chunk_text": "I fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2025'06'12Part I : Sec. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 12.06.20254A\n\n6. Grid Connection & Operation\n\n(ii) The Generating Facility shall include anti - islanding Protection and other safeguards to prevent safety risks to the grid, Distribution Licensee\u2019s Personnel and the general public. 7. Environment\n\nThe Exempted Person shall comply with all applicable Environmental Laws in Sri Lanka, subject to any exemptions or grace periods which may be granted to the Exempted Person under such Environmental Laws for compliance.\n\n8. Safety\n\nThe Exempted Person shall take all reasonable and necessary steps to protect persons, Generating Facilitiy, property and equipment from injury, damage and hazards. Additionally, all necessary safety precaustions must be taken during the decommissioning of the generating facilitiy.\n\n9. Insurance\n\nThe Exempted Person shall adopt and implement reasonable and prudent policies in relation to the management and insurance of risks associated with the Generating Facility.\n\n10. Modification of the Certificate of Exemption\n\nThe Commission reserves the right to amend or modify any conditions of this Notice.\n\n11. Offence\n\nAny Exempted Person who fails to comply with or contravenes, any of the conditions set forth herein shall be deemed to have committed an offence under the Act.\n\n12. Repeals and savings\n\nThe Certificates of Exemptions published under Section 10 (3) of the Act in Gazette Extraordinary No. 2006/19 dated February 14, 2017 and Gazette Extraordinary No. 1961/50 dated March 9, 2018, are hereby repealed and shall cease to apply to all schemes presently in operation. All such schemes presently in operation shall come within this Certificate of Exemption in a manner corresponding to the technical configurations provided herein.\n\nEOG 06 - 0110\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA."
